+ {t:'progressive web apps', w:1.4, k:['pwa','progressive web app','installable website','install on phone','add to home screen','works offline','offline website','app like website','website that feels like an app','do i need an app or a website','app store or website'],
+  a:`A PWA is a site your customer can install to their home screen. It opens full screen with your icon, keeps working when the signal drops, and needs no app store approval or download.<br><br>For most businesses it does the job a native app was wanted for, at a fraction of the cost and with nothing to submit to Apple or Google. Tell us what you want it to do and we will say honestly whether a PWA covers it.`},
+
+ {t:'frameworks and stack', w:1.4, k:['next.js','vue','svelte','which framework','what framework do you use','do you use react','server side rendering','ssr','static site','jamstack'],
+  a:`Most builds are hand written HTML, CSS and JavaScript with a Supabase backend, because that is what keeps a site fast and cheap to run.<br><br>We use Next.js where a framework genuinely earns its place: a large catalogue, server rendering that changes what ranks, or an app with real routing. We will not add one just to have a framework on the invoice.`},
+
+ {t:'3D and WebGL', w:1.35, k:['three.js','3d on website','interactive 3d','3d model on site','spinning product','rotate product','shader'],
+  a:`Real time 3D in the browser, built with Three.js and WebGL. A rotating product, an interactive scene, a globe.<br><br>It is used where it carries the idea rather than decorating the page, and it always ships with a lighter fallback so a mid range Android is not asked to render something it cannot. Examples are live in the <a href="index.html#work">Work</a> section.`},
+
+ {t:'site migration', w:1.4, k:['will i lose rankings if i migrate','migrate','rankings after migration','migrate my site','migration','move my website','transfer website','switch host','move off wordpress','move off wix','move off shopify','will i lose my rankings','keep my rankings','redirects','301'],
+  a:`Yes, and the ranking question is the right one to ask first. We audit what you have, keep the URLs and content already earning traffic, and rebuild the rest with redirects mapped before launch.<br><br>Done that way your rankings carry over instead of resetting on launch day. Done carelessly they do not, which is why the audit comes before any code.`},
+
+ {t:'point of sale', w:1.5, k:['pos for my shop','billing counter','shop billing','pos system','billing system','counter software','cash register','till','billing software','invoice at counter','receipt printer'],
+  a:`POS and billing that writes into the same records as everything else: every sale moves your stock count, feeds the day's takings and lands in the reports.<br><br>Barcode scanning works from a phone camera, so there is no separate scanner to buy. It runs on a counter tablet and on your phone. Full breakdown on the <a href="business-software.html#systems">Business Software</a> page.`},
+
+ {t:'clinic systems', w:1.45, k:['clinic software','patient records','doctor software','patient management','medical records','appointment system for clinic','hospital software','dental clinic','physio'],
+  a:`Appointments, visit history and patient records in one system, with proper role based access so the receptionist and the doctor see different things.<br><br>Bookings confirm on WhatsApp where patients actually read them, and reminders go the same way. It is one of nine systems on the <a href="business-software.html#systems">Business Software</a> page.`},
+
+ {t:'gym systems', w:1.5, k:['gym membership software','membership software','gym system','gym software','gym management','membership system','member management','fitness centre software','track memberships','renewals','lapsed members','attendance for gym'],
+  a:`Memberships, renewals, attendance and the lapsed member list that tells you who stopped coming before they stop paying.<br><br>We have built for gyms and martial arts academies already running live. See the <a href="business-software.html#systems">Business Software</a> page for what the owner side actually looks like.`},
+
+ {t:'school and LMS', w:1.45, k:['school management system','school system','academy management','school software','lms','learning management','tuition software','academy software','student portal','past papers','syllabus','notes portal','online institute','coaching centre','attendance for school','fee management','result system'],
+  a:`Syllabus architecture, notes and past paper libraries, student portals and staff records. We have built these for schools, academies and tuition platforms that are live now.<br><br>The teacher or admin gets a panel to publish notices, upload papers and read enquiries without messaging anyone. Examples in the <a href="index.html#work">Work</a> section.`},
+
+ {t:'stock and inventory', w:1.4, k:['stock system','inventory system','stock management','reorder level','stock alert','supplier ledger','stock count','running out of stock'],
+  a:`Live stock across one branch or many, where every sale and purchase moves the count so the number on screen is the number on the shelf.<br><br>When a line drops under its reorder level you hear about it before a customer does. Supplier ledgers, purchase entry, returns and damage records come with it.`},
+
+ {t:'quotations and CRM', w:1.4, k:['quotation system','quote software','customer records','client database','follow up system','sales pipeline','job tracking','job cards','work orders'],
+  a:`Customer records with full history, quotes generated from your own pricing logic, and job tracking that shows what is in progress, who owns it and what is overdue.<br><br>Built around how you already work rather than making your team bend to someone else's workflow.`},
+
+ {t:'staff and roles', w:1.4, k:['staff records','employee management','attendance system','shift management','staff logins','role based access','who can see what','limit access','manager login'],
+  a:`Three tier access so the counter, the manager and the owner each see only what they should. Staff records, shifts and attendance sit in the same system.<br><br>Every action is logged, so if a price changed or a record was deleted there is a trail showing who did it and when.`},
+
+ {t:'exports and reports', w:1.4, k:['export to excel','excel me export','download in excel','give data to accountant','export data','csv export','excel export','download data','accountant','audit trail','send to accountant','print report','monthly report from system'],
+  a:`Any table becomes a spreadsheet in one click: sales, customers, stock, attendance. Your accountant gets a file instead of a screenshot.<br><br>Reports are chosen with you before anything is built, so the panel opens on the four or five figures that actually decide your day.`},
+
+ {t:'WhatsApp chatbot', w:1.5, k:['whatsapp chatbot','bot on whatsapp','chatbot on whatsapp','reply on whatsapp automatically','auto reply whatsapp','whatsapp assistant'],
+  a:`The same trained assistant, answering on WhatsApp instead of only on your site. It knows your services, hours and policies, qualifies the enquiry, then hands the real ones to you with the context attached.<br><br>Most clients run both, because the site catches strangers and WhatsApp catches the people who already have your number.`},
+
+ {t:'chatbot languages', w:1.5, k:['urdu chatbot','does the bot speak urdu','multilingual bot','bilingual bot','arabic bot','bot language','which languages does the bot'],
+  a:`English, Urdu and Roman Urdu. It replies in whichever of the three the customer opened with, so nobody has to switch to please the software.<br><br>Other languages are possible. Tell us which ones your customers actually use and we will scope it.`},
+
+ {t:'chatbot integrations', w:1.4, k:['bot api','api key','connect bot to crm','bot integration','integrate chatbot','bot to my system','custom bot','bot connected to database','openai key','use my own api key'],
+  a:`Beyond the site assistant, we build bots wired into your own systems and third party services through their APIs, including your own keys where you would rather own the account and the billing.<br><br>Qualified conversations get written into your records rather than ending in a chat window nobody exports.`},
+
+ {t:'calling agent detail', w:1.4, k:['record calls','accent','agent accent','which language does the agent speak','connect to my calendar','calendar integration','books into calendar','crm for calls'],
+  a:`Language and accent are chosen to match the people you are actually calling. Calls are recorded and kept alongside the transcript and the outcome, so you can hear what happened rather than read a summary of it.<br><br>Bookings write straight into your calendar and outcomes into your CRM.`},
+
+ {t:'wedding and event films', w:1.55, k:['shadi ki video','shadi ki video edit','wedding ki video','event ki video','shadi shoot','wedding video','wedding film','shadi video','event video','event film','mehndi','barat','walima','birthday video','conference video','wedding editing','event coverage edit'],
+  a:`Long form event work cut for the people who were actually there. You get a full film to keep and a short version that works on a feed without needing context.<br><br>Speeches and vows are kept clean and audible, colour is matched across whatever lighting the venue had, and your raw footage comes back with the delivery. It is one of the seven formats on the <a href="video-editing.html#formats">Video Editing</a> page.`},
+
+ {t:'colour and sound', w:1.4, k:['colour grading','color grading','grading','colour correction','color correction','audio cleanup','fix bad audio','noise removal','mixing','music bed','sound mix'],
+  a:`Real colour and audio work, not filter presets. Colour is matched across a whole cut so it reads as one piece, and audio gets levels, cleanup, music and effects placed deliberately.<br><br>Bad audio is the one thing an edit cannot fully rescue, so record somewhere quiet if you can. Everything else we can work with.`},
+
+ {t:'explainer videos', w:1.4, k:['explainer','explainer video','how it works video','product demo video','tutorial video','training video','animated explainer','screen recording video'],
+  a:`Structured to teach one thing clearly rather than list ten features. Usually motion graphics over narration, or a screen recording cut so the viewer never waits.<br><br>These work well as the video on a landing page, where the job is to answer one objection before someone leaves.`},
+
+ {t:'naming', w:1.5, k:['naming','name for my business','business name','brand name','help me name','what should i call it','company name ideas','name and logo together'],
+  a:`Yes, where the business does not have a name yet. It runs before the logo, because designing a mark for a name you are unsure about wastes both.<br><br>Say what the business does and who it is for on ${WAL} and we will tell you whether naming is worth scoping separately or folding into the identity.`},
+
+ {t:'pitch decks', w:1.4, k:['pitch deck','investor deck','presentation design','slide deck','powerpoint design','proposal design','sales deck','ppt design'],
+  a:`Slides built to the same identity as everything else you send out, so the deck does not look like it came from a different company than the website.<br><br>Company profiles and proposals too. Send what you have, even if it is rough, and we will tell you what it needs.`},
+
+ {t:'signage and print', w:1.5, k:['signage design','shop signboard','signboard design','board design','signage','shop board','shop frontage','banner design','standee','pana flex','flex design','hoarding','billboard','vehicle branding','print ready','bleed','cmyk'],
+  a:`Signboards, shop frontage, banners, standees and vehicle branding, designed with real print constraints so nothing arrives from the press looking different to the screen.<br><br>Everything is delivered print ready with bleed and marks, in CMYK, at the size your printer actually asked for. See <a href="design-and-ads.html#design">Design and Ads</a>.`},
+
+ {t:'brand guidelines', w:1.35, k:['brand guidelines','brand book','style guide','brand manual','usage rules','clear space','how do i keep my brand consistent','asset kit'],
+  a:`Colour, type, spacing and tone written down so the next person who touches your brand cannot quietly break it. Hex, RGB and CMYK values, type pairing with weights, logo clear space and minimum sizes.<br><br>It matters most when you are not the one placing the logo: a printer, an intern or another agency all work from the same document.`},
+
+ {t:'influencer work', w:1.45, k:['influencer','influencers','collab','collaboration','ugc creator','creator','brand ambassador','find influencers','influencer marketing'],
+  a:`Briefing, scheduling and getting usable assets back, so a collaboration produces something you can actually run rather than a post that disappears in a day.<br><br>We do not maintain a roster or take a cut from creators. If you already have people in mind we will handle the coordination and the edit.`},
+
+ {t:'ad audits', w:1.5, k:['audit my ads','review my ads','ads not working','ads not converting','wasting money on ads','my ads stopped working','fix my campaigns','why are my ads expensive','high cpc','bad leads'],
+  a:`We audit what is there first: structure, audiences, creative and what the numbers actually say. Then we tell you honestly whether it needs restructuring or just better creative.<br><br>Sometimes the campaign is fine and the landing page is the problem. Since the site and the ads are built by the same studio, we can say which it is instead of blaming the other half.`},
+
+ {t:'ad spend and accounts', w:1.4, k:['who pays meta','do you take a cut','percentage of ad spend','commission on ads','do i keep the pixel','minimum ad budget'],
+  a:`You pay Meta and Google directly from your own ad account, so you keep the pixel, the data and the history if you ever change agency.<br><br>We are paid for the work, not a slice of your spend, which means there is no incentive for us to tell you to spend more than you should.`},
+
+ {t:'local SEO', w:1.4, k:['rank in karachi','near me searches','local search','service area','google business profile'],
+  a:`Every build ships with the local signals set up for the people searching nearest to you. Ongoing local work, including Google Business Profile optimisation and location pages, is scoped separately because it is monthly work.<br><br>The studio is in Karachi, so local search here is something we have done repeatedly rather than read about.`},
+
+ {t:'technical SEO', w:1.35, k:['technical seo','lcp','cls','inp','page speed','site speed','crawl','indexing','not indexed','structured data','rich snippets','robots txt'],
+  a:`Titles and canonicals, schema markup, Open Graph, sitemap, robots and Search Console are set up at launch on every build, not months later. Core Web Vitals are measured and fixed as the site is written.<br><br>Technical fixes can register in days. Competitive commercial terms take three to six months, and anyone promising page one in a month is describing something other than SEO.`}
 
